1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,740
You don’t need to be a student.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:04,340
Or a teacher.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,240
Or a scientist.

4
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:09,540
You just need to be curious.

5
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:20,029
İDÜ Lab is open to anyone who has ever wondered how the world works.

6
00:00:28,775 --> 00:00:30,615
Start with the science guide.

7
00:00:30,675 --> 00:00:32,815
It begins with everyday questions.

8
00:00:32,875 --> 00:00:37,015
What will your phone’s keyboard suggest next?

9
00:00:37,075 --> 00:00:41,215
Which record in a ledger was changed later?

10
00:00:41,275 --> 00:00:45,415
How do you keep an island lit after sunset?

11
00:00:45,475 --> 00:00:58,673
Each question opens a world you can play, from language models and blockchain to clean energy and DNA.

12
00:00:59,283 --> 00:01:03,123
Every week there’s a new science mission, open to everyone.

13
00:01:03,183 --> 00:01:08,823
Take TRAPPIST-1: one star, real catalogue data, and planets you can measure.

14
00:01:08,883 --> 00:01:13,923
You learn what the data can tell you, and what it cannot.

15
00:01:13,983 --> 00:01:17,323
That’s science, honestly told.

16
00:01:17,383 --> 00:01:23,523
Then keep exploring in Planet hunt, one of the ten main worlds.

17
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:29,182
Or find your latitude with an astrolabe.

18
00:01:29,792 --> 00:01:31,432
Explore the corners.

19
00:01:31,492 --> 00:01:35,832
The museum corner.

20
00:01:35,892 --> 00:01:42,132
Scientists from Türkiye.

21
00:01:42,192 --> 00:01:48,432
Mimar Sinan’s architecture.

22
00:01:48,492 --> 00:01:54,732
Science Bridges between Türkiye and countries such as Japan, Germany and Hungary.

23
00:01:54,792 --> 00:01:59,690
And life-skills labs for planning, budgeting and coping with stress.

24
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:11,340
Play your way, in twenty-five languages.

25
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:17,740
On any phone, tablet or computer, with nothing to install.

26
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:24,040
Not sure where to begin? Kuark suggests games from your age and interests, and explains why.

27
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:30,198
Questions? Ask in the forum, right next to every game.

28
00:02:30,708 --> 00:02:32,048
So, who is İDÜ Lab for?

29
00:02:32,108 --> 00:02:34,048
Anyone who asks why.

30
00:02:34,108 --> 00:02:38,048
Including you.

31
00:02:38,108 --> 00:02:46,470
And if you’re a science communicator, an artist or an athlete, Guest Studio can help you build a game of your own.

